The BWMORP algorithm as implemented in Matlab is utilized to extract a skeletal image of the human hand and then the furthest endpoint of the skeleton is selected to represent the fingertip [18] . An example of this procedure is shown in Figure 1 . When this fingertip is detected, the coordinates of the pixel are known as well. 
